 {"step_by_step_thinking": "First, we need to calculate the patient's ideal body weight (IBW) using the Hamwi-Benneth equation for men: IBW = 50 + (0.91 x height in cm) - (0.366 x age in years). Then, we'll calculate the patient's adjusted body weight (ABW) using the adjusted body weight formula: ABW = IBW + (0.4 x (actual body weight - IBW)).

IBW = 50 + (0.91 x 180 cm) - (0.366 x 48 years) = 73.6 kg

ABW = 73.6 kg + (0.4 x (107 kg - 73.6 kg)) = 101.2 kg", "answer": "101.2 kg"}
